# The same support ticket, one commit earlier: the key arriving rather than
# being edited around. `git diff` prefixes every added line with `+`, which is
# neither whitespace nor a line ending, so none of the three steps from the
# header to the body could cross it -- not the separator, not the `Proc-Type:`
# and `DEK-Info:` lines, not the body's own indentation. The encrypted layout
# is what makes all three load-bearing at once.
#
# An added *plain* key was reported before this, and by accident: `+` is in the
# base64 alphabet, so `+QUJD...` reads as a body line that starts one byte early.
# Nothing chose that, and it does not reach the encrypted layout.
#
# Same fabricated body as the other five, base64 of ordinary ASCII.
#
# Produced by `git diff --cached`, not written by hand: git 2.55.0, 2026-09-19.

diff --git a/deploy/tls.key b/deploy/tls.key
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0148383
--- /dev/null
+++ b/deploy/tls.key
